/*
The Needle - a Builder structure oriented towards the heart of Saggitarius A*. Situated at the exact center of the plate.
KHAKRIKITA-KHA - Crashed shoaler arkship shard, center of their activities on the plate.


PEOPLE:

baldies, monkies, humans - Generally scattered at random from timeframes in the last two hundred years (2100-2300),
which roughly lines up with the earliest period anyone on the plate knows of the Signal exposure reaching Earth.


CONCEPTS:

The Plate - the section of the ruined ringworld that the map is set on. One segment among dozens. Atmosphere is
poisonous but breathable for short periods. Outdoor gear is usually a warm coat or cloak, a mask to avoid breathing the
ringfall, and a rifle to fend off the thieves.

Builders - the dead or absent species that built the ringworld. Long, spindly, six-limbed creatures based on their
iconography. Technology is universally psionically active, implying a species-wide susceptibility/resistance to informatic
infection.

Lapse - the frequent changes in the universe, every few hours, where things reset and time jumps. Seems to be associated
with the rotation of the black hole and the frequency of the signal emissions. May be actively preventing people escaping
the ring.

Lapsed - people who have become aware of the noncontinuity of their existence, and preserve memory over lapses. (player characters)

Semiotic decay - aka bleed or blur. Psionic overexposure causes a decay in objective meaning and makes it easier and more
dangerous to manifest psionic phenomena in that area. Progressive semiotic decay can lead to semiotic collapse, but is
generally recoverable prior to that point.

Semiotic collapse - the semiotic decay of a volume reaches a critical point and objective meaning undergoes complete collapse.
Reality becomes entirely malleable and separate existence becomes difficult or impossible.

Signal infection - exposure of a complex system to the pulses that are emitted by Saggitarius A* on intervals causes a
progressive degenerative condition as the brain is 'adjusted'. The majority of cases end with short-term disorders and
no long-term effects, others cause permanent restructuring and psionic latencies, others cause madness or immediate
semiotic collapse.

Erosion - the cumulative impact of semiotic decay over time among the Lapsed. Trauma from psionic overexposure is not
subject to resets and can manifest as derangements.

Ringfall - detritus from the orbiting husks of ships that have orbits too fast to crash into the ring - forms into the
ashen drifts that make up the majority of the terrain of the plate. Sifted and refined into trace resources, metal,
protein, organic molecules.

Upswell/downswell - gravity storms caused by disturbances within Saggitarius A*.

Dustsuckers - Adapted ramshackle vehicles maintained by communities and sent out to harvest after ringfall.

Cipher - people, animals and machines that have undergone semiotic collapse or are so heavily infected by signal exposure
that they are malicious and unstable.

Ciphered - the process of beocoming a cipher, or an adjective describing someone unstable or malicious from signal exposure
or semiotic decay.


IDLE NOTES

- Wound system to record serious injuries across lapses.

*/
